      "notes": "K2's own: a Thread panel to talk to one agent inside a widget. K2Thread.mount(el, {look: 'chamfer' or 'glass', address: 'handle::host'}) then panel.open(address, label), panel.post(text), panel.setLook(look), panel.destroy(). chamfer is K2's Thread with chamfered corners in the Garden theme's colours; glass is K2 Companion's round look and palette. Both: bubbles with author and time, choice cards, Enter sends (Shift+Enter a new line), the working tab (the agent's Thread turn in k2-activity@1's words, never a guess), stick-to-bottom scrolling with a new-messages pill, a narrow layout, file chips and data: images for attachments. Needs thread:read and thread:post (agents:read for names, activity:read for the working tab; K2 loads k2-activity@1 for you). Add marked and dompurify for markdown bodies."
